# 🧰 RegexPilot Feature Toolkit

### 🧩 Visual Pattern Builder

🧱 Drag character classes, anchors, groups and lookarounds onto the visual canvas.

### 🎯 Pattern Inspector

🔍 Select individual nodes and fine-tune their configuration without manually editing the entire expression.

### 🌳 Breakdown Tree

📖 See a structured plain-English explanation of the regex and understand how individual components interact.

### 🧪 Live Match Testing

✨ Paste test content and immediately inspect matching sections and capture groups.

### 🔄 Visual Replace Builder

🛠️ Build replacement expressions visually using literals, references and transformation blocks.

### 🌐 Authentic Regex Engines

⚙️ Test patterns against engines associated with the target language rather than relying on a generic JavaScript approximation.

### 📚 Pattern Library

🗂️ Store useful expressions such as email validation, URLs, IPv4 addresses, ISO dates, password rules and log-processing patterns.

---

# 🌐 Multi-Language Regex Environment

Regex behavior can vary between programming languages, which makes testing against the intended flavor especially useful.

🟨 **JavaScript / TypeScript** → JavaScriptCore-based workflow.

🐍 **Python** → Python regex support including standard and extended capabilities.

☕ **Java** → Java-compatible regex engine testing.

🔷 **C# / .NET** → .NET regex compatibility.

💎 **Ruby** → Ruby/Onigmo-based behavior.

🐘 **PHP** → PCRE2-oriented pattern testing.

🐹 **Go / RE2** → Go-compatible regular expressions.

🦀 **Rust** → Rust regex workflow.

🪶 **Perl** → Perl-compatible pattern testing.

🍎 **Swift** → NSRegularExpression-based workflow.

🗄️ **MySQL / PostgreSQL** → Database-oriented regex environments.

🐚 **Shell** → POSIX-style grep, sed and awk workflows.

---

